-mktg/_next/static/media/favicon-48x48.3bffc684.png" type="image/png" sizes="48x48"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/b2b-mktg/_next/static/media/apple-touch-icon-180x180.7ea10466.png" sizes="180x180"/><style>
:root {
  --font-body: RoobertPRO, AktivGroteskVF, sans-serif;
  --font-header: var(--font-body);
  --font-link: var(--font-body);
  --font-display: Tartuffo, Changa, PlayfairDisplay, serif;
}

[lang^='ar'] {
--font-body: AktivGroteskVF, RoobertPRO, sans-serif;
--font-display: Changa, Tartuffo, PlayfairDisplay, serif;
}

[lang^='vi'] {
--font-body: AktivGroteskVF, RoobertPRO, sans-serif;
--font-display: PlayfairDisplay, Tartuffo, Changa, serif;
}

/*
 * Vietnamese and Thai scripts stack diacritical marks above and below characters.
 * These overrides ensure a minimum line-height of 1.6 is applied to headings for these locales,
 * preventing diacritical clipping on heading text.
 *
 * Non-layered CSS (injected via <style> tag) wins over @layer-based Tailwind utilities,
 * so these rules correctly override any leading-[Xpx] utility classes on headings.
 *
 * Per i18n/l10n guidelines: https://www.notion.so/fresha-app/b99f9dc9fb4d44bab44de3da46478dac#33072a978ef080a2ad7ef010eee78293
 * - Vietnamese: 1.6 minimum, 1.8 recommended
 * - Thai: 1.6 minimum, 1.8 recommended
 */
[lang^='vi'] h1,
[lang^='vi'] h2,
[lang^='vi'] h3,
[lang^='vi'] h4,
[lang^='vi'] h5,
[lang^='vi'] h6,
[lang^='th'] h1,
[lang^='th'] h2,
[lang^='th'] h3,
[lang^='th'] h4,
[lang^='th'] h5,
[lang^='th'] h6 {
  line-height: 1.6;
}

